-- allium: 3
--
-- pellucid: a Pixelfed client whose user interface is PureScript (Halogen)
-- in a Tauri 2 webview and whose network and secret handling is Rust. It
-- speaks the API that pixelfed-rn speaks to stock Pixelfed servers today,
-- so it can be used against pixelfed.social and any other instance before
-- a Pellucid server exists. This file is the contract the code is held
-- to: where the code and this file disagree, this file records the
-- intended behaviour and section IMPLEMENTATION STATUS says which rules
-- are built.
--
-- RELATION TO OTHER SPECS. None yet. A server spec (ActivityPub, storage,
-- moderation) is a separate future file; nothing in this file assumes it.
-- The fleet side of the test instance is one NixOS module
-- (pixelfed-lab.nix) and is described under surface LabInstance.
--
-- REVISIONS. Written 2026-11-09 against the second batch of the port: the
-- rename to Pellucid, the login and feed slice from the first batch, and
-- the post detail and profile screens added in the second. Revised the
-- same day for the third batch: notifications, compose with media upload,
-- deletion of the viewer's own post, and PKCE on login.
--
-- FACTS THIS SPEC IS WRITTEN AGAINST, checked 2026-11-09 in the source of
-- pixelfed/pixelfed (dev) and pixelfed/pixelfed-rn (main):
--   - config/cors.php sets allowed_origins to [] unless the operator sets
--     PF_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS. Only /api/v1/apps and /api/v2/instance set
--     Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * by hand. Timelines, /oauth/token and
--     verify_credentials send no CORS header. A page in a browser cannot
--     log in to a stock instance; a native HTTP client can.
--   - The query flag _pe=1 (PF_API_ENTITY_KEY) selects StatusService::get,
--     the Pixelfed entity with pf_type, content_text, liked_by,
--     comments_disabled, place and taggedPeople. Without it
--     StatusService::getMastodon strips those keys and adds replies_count.
--   - POST /api/v1/statuses/{id}/bookmark and /unbookmark ignore _pe and
--     return the Mastodon entity. favourite and unfavourite honour it.
--   - Login is OAuth 2 authorization code through Laravel Passport 13.10
--     on league/oauth2-server 9.4.1 (composer.lock): GET
--     /api/nodeinfo/2.0.json (software.name must be pixelfed, version at
--     least 0.12.3), POST /api/v1/apps form-encoded with client_name,
--     redirect_uris (newline separated, any URI accepted, urldecoded once
--     more on the server), scopes, website; GET /oauth/authorize with
--     client_id, redirect_uri, response_type=code, scope; POST /oauth/token
--     form-encoded with grant_type=authorization_code, code, client_id,
--     client_secret, redirect_uri, scope; GET
--     /api/v1/accounts/verify_credentials?_pe=1. Both OAuth routes are
--     throttled to 10 requests a minute.
--   - PKCE is accepted: league 9 stores code_challenge and
--     code_challenge_method (plain or S256) from /oauth/authorize in the
--     authorization code and refuses /oauth/token without a matching
--     code_verifier whenever a challenge was stored. /api/v1/apps creates
--     confidential clients (a 40-character secret, personal_access_client
--     and password_client false), and Passport demands the secret of a
--     confidential client at /oauth/token, so PKCE adds protection against
--     code interception without removing the secret.
--   - Pixelfed registers Passport's routes by hand in routes/web.php: POST
--     /oauth/token and GET /oauth/authorize are public; POST and DELETE
--     /oauth/authorize (the out-of-band consent form), /oauth/tokens,
--     DELETE /oauth/tokens/{id} and the client routes sit behind auth:web,
--     the browser session. There is no RFC 7009 /oauth/revoke. POST
--     /api/v1.1/accounts/apps-and-applications/{id}/revoke needs the
--     security:write scope and answers 422 for the token making the
--     request. A client cannot revoke its own token.
--   - Timelines paginate by the Link header, <url>; rel="next",<url>;
--     rel="prev", with max_id and min_id already in the URLs. The URLs are
--     absolute and built from config('app.url').
--   - GET /api/v1/statuses/{id}/context honours _pe, returns up to 100
--     descendants and sends no Link header.
--   - GET /api/v1/accounts/{id}/statuses honours _pe, max_id, min_id and
--     limit (1..100) and sends no Link header. A locked account the viewer
--     does not follow yields [].
--   - GET /api/v1/accounts/relationships takes id[] (at most 20) and
--     returns RelationshipService::get entries: id, following, followed_by,
--     blocking, muting, muting_notifications, requested, domain_blocking,
--     showing_reblogs, endorsed. The viewer's own id yields no entry.
--   - POST /api/v1/accounts/{id}/follow and /unfollow return the same
--     Relationship shape; follow on a locked account sets requested.
--   - POST /api/v1/statuses honours _pe. Validation: status at most
--     max_caption_length (default 500), media_ids an array of at most
--     max_album_length (default 4), visibility in private, unlisted,
--     public, direct, spoiler_text at most 140, comments_disabled boolean.
--     With neither media_ids nor in_reply_to_id it answers 403 "Empty
--     statuses are not allowed". A reply comes back as the created status.
--     pixelfed-rn sends these as query parameters; Laravel reads a JSON
--     body the same way.
--   - DELETE /api/v1/statuses/{id} returns the deleted status.
--   - POST /api/v2/media is multipart with file (or file[]) and an
--     optional description (at most max_altext_length). The file must
--     match pixelfed.media_types (default image/jpeg, image/jpg, image/png,
--     image/gif; pixelfed.social adds video/mp4) and be at most
--     pixelfed.max_photo_size kilobytes (default 15000). 429 when the
--     account's daily upload count is spent, 403 when its storage is full.
--     The answer is MediaTransformer with url null and preview_url the
--     stored file plus ?v=. PUT /api/v1/media/{id} with description answers
--     with the same transformer. GET /api/v1.1/compose/settings returns
--     allowed_media_types (an array, or one comma-joined string),
--     max_caption_length, max_file_size in kilobytes,
--     max_media_attachments, max_altext_length and default_scope.
--   - GET /api/v1/notifications honours _pe, caps limit at 40 (default
--     20), pages by max_id, min_id and since_id with a Link header, and
--     filters by types[] in mention, reblog, follow, favourite (no comment
--     filter). NotificationTransformer maps verbs: dm to direct, follow,
--     mention, reblog and share to share, like to favourite, comment,
--     admin.user.modlog.comment to modlog, tagged, story:react,
--     story:comment. Fields: id, type, created_at, account (the actor),
--     relationship (when the actor is someone else), status (always the
--     Pixelfed entity through StatusService::get, whatever _pe says),
--     direct { conversation_id, message_id }, modlog { id, url }, tagged
--     { username, post_url, status_id, profile_id }. Which status: the
--     liked or shared post for like and share (SharePipeline stores
--     reblog_of_id), the comment itself for comment, the mentioning post
--     for mention, none for follow (the item is a Profile) and tagged (the
--     item is a MediaTag).
--   - Counters have shipped as numbers, as strings and as null.
--   - liked_by is { username: null, others: false } when there is nobody
--     to show.
--   - Status created_at is Y-m-d\TH:i:s.vP rewritten to ...Z (three
--     fractional digits); Account created_at is Carbon toJSON (six).
--   - pixelfed-rn is 23,382 lines of TypeScript across 85 screens and
--     roughly 110 endpoints over /api/v1, /api/v1.1, /api/v1.2, /api/v2,
--     /api/admin and pixelfed.org's open server directory. It stores the
--     token in MMKV, unencrypted.
--   - Tauri 2.12: app.withGlobalTauri exposes window.__TAURI__.core.invoke
--     and .event.listen with no npm package; application commands need no
--     capability entry; the IPC needs connect-src ipc: http://ipc.localhost
--     in the CSP; Linux codegen reads the first .png in bundle.icon at
--     compile time and fails without it; build.beforeDevCommand runs from
--     the directory above src-tauri when no package.json exists and waits
--     for the script only when given { script, wait: true }. invoke(cmd,
--     Uint8Array, { headers }) sends the bytes as the raw IPC body; a
--     command declared with a tauri::ipc::Request argument reads them as
--     InvokeBody::Raw and reads the headers.
--   - nixpkgs nixos-unstable packages Pixelfed 0.12.9 with a
--     services.pixelfed module (domain, secretFile, settings as .env
--     key=value, nginx vhost, local MySQL and Redis, pixelfed-manage
--     wrapper for artisan). user:create takes --name --username --email
--     --password --is_admin --confirm_email; user:admin takes a username.
--   - The registry package set 81.11.4 with purs 0.15.16 and spago 1.0.5
--     (both from purescript-overlay) builds Halogen 7.0.0, routing-duplex
--     0.7.0, argonaut-codecs 9.1.0, aff-promise 4.0.0, web-file 4.0.0 and
--     arraybuffer-types 3.0.2.
--
-- Decisions taken 2026-11-09:
--
--   D1. SCOPE. A client for the existing Pixelfed protocol first. The
--       server is a later project with its own spec. Everything the client
--       needs is reached through the endpoints pixelfed-rn already uses.
--
--   D2. THE SPLIT. Rust (crate pixelfed-core, no UI, no Tauri dependency)
--       owns the OAuth dance, the token, the authenticated transport and
--       the validation of every URL the token travels to. PureScript owns
--       the entities, the decoders, the screens and the state. The Tauri
--       crate is an adapter between the two and holds no protocol logic.
--
--   D3. THE TOKEN NEVER CROSSES THE BRIDGE. The webview receives
--       SessionSummary (domain, account id, acct) and never the access
--       token, the client secret or the refresh token. This is what the
--       CORS fact makes free: since Rust must make the requests anyway,
--       the token has no reason to exist in JavaScript.
--
--   D4. THE TOKEN GOES ONLY TO /api/ PATHS ON THE LOGGED-IN ORIGIN. A
--       request path must start with /api/. A pagination cursor is used
--       only after Rust parses it, checks scheme https, the same host and
--       port as the session's domain, and a path under /api/. The upload
--       goes to the fixed path /api/v2/media on the same origin.
--
--   D5. HTTPS ONLY. Domain is a validated host; its base URL is always
--       https. There is no insecure mode and none is planned; the test
--       instance gets a real certificate instead (D16).
--
--   D6. NO HTML IS RENDERED AS HTML. Captions are content_text. When a
--       server omits it the HTML content is reduced to text by stripping
--       tags and decoding the common entities, and that text is set as a
--       text node. innerHTML is not used anywhere. Hashtags and mentions
--       will be linked from the tags and mentions arrays, not by trusting
--       the server's markup.
--
--   D7. NO NPM. The frontend is spago packages plus two hand-written
--       foreign modules: src/App/Backend/Tauri.js, which reaches
--       window.__TAURI__ because app.withGlobalTauri is on, and
--       src/Util/File.js, which calls file.arrayBuffer(). Everything
--       foreign is listed in contract ForeignBudget.
--
--   D8. PIXELFED ENTITIES, LENIENTLY DECODED. Every read sends _pe=1.
--       Decoders default every field Pixelfed has ever omitted or nulled,
--       read counters from numbers and strings, and keep unknown
--       visibilities, pf_types, media types and notification verbs as
--       data rather than failing, so one new server value cannot blank a
--       feed. A notification whose actor or status cannot be decoded keeps
--       its row with that part missing.
--
--   D9. THE SERVER IS THE TRUTH FOR TOGGLES. A like or bookmark shows the
--       old state until the server answers. The answer is merged by rule:
--       the favourite endpoints return the Pixelfed entity, which replaces
--       ours; the bookmark endpoints return the Mastodon entity, from
--       which only the bookmarked flag is taken. A reply or a deletion
--       adjusts the reply count locally by one, since the server does not
--       return the parent.
--
--   D10. ONE LOGIN FLOW, TWO REDIRECTS. The desktop shell binds a one-shot
--        listener on 127.0.0.1 and registers http://127.0.0.1:PORT/callback
--        as the redirect URI; the state parameter is a random UUID checked
--        on return; unrelated requests to the port are answered 404 and
--        ignored. A mobile shell will register a custom scheme through
--        tauri-plugin-deep-link and hand the same code to the same
--        login_finish. Nothing else about login differs per platform.
--
--   D11. A FRESH CLIENT PER LOGIN. Each login registers a new OAuth
--        client, as pixelfed-rn does, because the redirect URI carries an
--        ephemeral port and because Pixelfed issues clients freely.
--
--   D12. SESSION STORAGE IS A SEAM. SecretStore is a trait. The desktop
--        implementation is a JSON file with mode 0600 under the app data
--        directory (com.harryprayiv.pellucid), written atomically. Mobile
--        implementations (Android Keystore, iOS Keychain) plug into the
--        same trait and are not built. The file holds the client secret as
--        well as the token (D19), so the mobile stores must protect both.
--
--   D13. LOGOUT IS LOCAL. It clears the store and the in-memory session
--        and emits session-changed with null. The server keeps the token
--        until it expires, because stock Pixelfed offers a client no way to
--        revoke the token it is using (KnownIssue no_token_revoke).
--
--   D14. PAGINATION FOLLOWS WHAT THE SERVER GIVES. Where a Link header
--        exists (timelines, notifications) the client stores the next URL
--        as an opaque Cursor and asks Rust to follow it (D4). Where none
--        exists (account statuses) the client pages by max_id = the last
--        id it holds, and an empty page ends the list. Pages are
--        deduplicated by id.
--
--   D15. THE GATE. scripts/check.fish runs purs-tidy check, spago build
--        --strict (warnings are errors), spago test, cargo fmt --check,
--        cargo clippy -D warnings and cargo test for the core crate, the
--        frontend bundle into dist/ (tauri::generate_context! panics at
--        compile time when frontendDist does not exist), and cargo clippy
--        -D warnings for the shell. The decoder tests run against fixtures
--        shaped like the server's transformers. Nothing is delivered with
--        a warning.
--
--   D16. A THROWAWAY INSTANCE ON BLADE. One NixOS module, lab.pixelfed,
--        turns on services.pixelfed with open registration, no email
--        verification, mail to the log, every ActivityPub switch off and
--        a Let's Encrypt certificate obtained by DNS-01, so the client
--        needs no exception for it. It is deleted by removing the import
--        and /var/lib/pixelfed.
--
--   D17. THE NAME. Pellucid, meaning transparently clear. The name claims
--        nothing by itself; the code, the gate and reproducible builds are
--        what make the claim. The identifier is com.harryprayiv.pellucid
--        and the OAuth client name shown on consent pages is Pellucid.
--
--   D18. RELEASE. AGPL-3.0-or-later. Not released until the port covers
--        what people use daily (surface list below) and the mobile shell
--        exists; the repository is private work until then.
--
--   D19. PKCE ALWAYS, SECRET STILL. Every login sends an S256 code
--        challenge from a fresh 32-byte verifier and sends the verifier
--        with the code. The server enforces the match because it stored
--        the challenge; nothing is configured per instance. The client
--        secret stays in the token request and in the session because
--        /api/v1/apps only issues confidential clients. What PKCE buys is
--        that a code taken off the loopback or deep-link redirect is
--        useless without the verifier, which never leaves Rust.
--
--   D20. MEDIA BYTES CROSS THE BRIDGE AS A RAW IPC BODY, ONCE. The UI
--        reads a picked File into an ArrayBuffer and invokes media_upload
--        with it as the body and the filename, MIME type and description
--        as percent-encoded headers. No base64, no temporary file, no path
--        handed to Rust; the shell never reads the filesystem for the
--        user. Rust refuses an empty body or one over 512 MiB before any
--        network, builds the multipart form and posts it with the token.
--        The server's preview_url is the thumbnail; the UI never makes an
--        object URL of its own.
--
--   D21. COMPOSE REQUIRES MEDIA AND UPLOADS FIRST. The server refuses a
--        status with no media, so Post is disabled until at least one
--        upload has finished and none is in flight or rejected. Each file
--        uploads when picked, in its own fiber. Limits come from
--        /api/v1.1/compose/settings and are applied before the upload
--        (count, size, type), with Pixelfed's stock defaults when that
--        call fails. Alt text is set with PUT /api/v1/media/{id} when its
--        field loses focus and again, for anything still unsaved, before
--        the status is created, so the attachment carries it from the
--        start.
--
--   D22. DELETING A POST TAKES TWO TAPS AND NO DIALOG. On the viewer's
--        own post the header shows a delete action; the first tap draws
--        a confirmation strip in the page, the second sends DELETE, and
--        success leaves the screen through history.back(). No window
--        .confirm(): a native dialog blocks the webview's IPC and cannot
--        be exercised headlessly.
--
-- IMPLEMENTATION STATUS at the third batch, 2026-11-09:
--
--   BUILT      D2, D3, D4, D5, D6, D7, D8, D9, D11, D13, D14, D15, D17,
--              D19, D20, D21, D22. Rules SessionRestored, LoginStarted,
--              LoginCompleted, LoginFailed, LoggedOut, RequestSent,
--              CursorFollowed, FeedLoads, FeedLoadsMore, ToggleApplied,
--              SensitiveRevealed, DetailOpens, ReplyPosted,
--              CommentDeleted, PostDeleted, ProfileOpens, FollowToggled,
--              ProfilePages, NotificationsLoad, NotificationsLoadMore,
--              NotificationOpened, ComposeOpens, MediaPicked,
--              MediaUploaded, AltTextSaved, PostCreated. Surfaces
--              LoginScreen, Feed, PostDetail, Profile, Notifications,
--              Compose, DevShell. The Rust core has 20 unit tests
--              including a loopback OAuth round trip, the RFC 7636
--              appendix B vector and the upload bounds; the decoders have
--              60 fixture checks; the bundled UI passes a 105-step
--              headless run against a mock of the Shell contract that
--              includes the raw-body upload (KnownIssue
--              smoke_harness_external).
--   PARTIAL    D10: the desktop redirect is built and tested; the deep
--              link branch is not written. D12: FileStore only. D16: the
--              module is written and parses; it has not been deployed.
--              The Tauri crate, including the media_upload command, type-
--              checks against the fetched sources of tauri 2.12.5 and
--              tauri-plugin-opener 2.7.2 by reading, not by compiling: the
--              environment the spec was written in has no GTK or WebKitGTK.
--   NOT BUILT  D18. Surfaces Search, Discover, DirectMessages, Settings,
--              Stories, Admin. Notification type filters, editing a
--              published post, deleting a post from the feed or the
--              profile grid, infinite scroll (the lists end in a Load more
--              button), blurhash placeholders, hashtag and mention links,
--              token revocation (impossible against stock Pixelfed), a Nix
--              package for the bundle and the desktop binary; the android
--              devShell has never been entered.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Given
------------------------------------------------------------

given {
    shell: Shell
    ui: Ui
    instance: Instance
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- External Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A Pixelfed server as the client meets it: one https origin, the
-- Mastodon-shaped API with Pixelfed's additions, OAuth 2 through Laravel
-- Passport.
external entity Instance {
    domain: Domain
    software: String
    version: String
    cors_open: Boolean       -- false on every stock instance
    public_timeline: Boolean
}

-- The operating system's browser, where the consent page is shown. The
-- app never embeds a login page of its own.
external entity SystemBrowser {
    opened_url: String?
}

-- A person with an account on an instance.
external entity Person {
    instance: Instance
    account_id: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A validated host. parse accepts an optional scheme, trailing slashes
-- and mixed case, rejects paths, queries, userinfo and hosts without a
-- dot (localhost excepted), lower-cases, and keeps an explicit port.
value Domain {
    host: String
    port: Integer?

    invariant BaseIsHttps {
        base_url = "https://" + host + (if port != null: ":" + port else "") + "/"
    }
}

-- An absolute URL taken from a Link header. The UI holds it as a string
-- it may not dereference; only Shell.api_follow may, after validation.
value Cursor {
    url: String
}

value ApiRequest {
    method: GET | POST | PUT | DELETE
    path: String            -- must start with /api/
    query: List<(String, String)>
    body: Json?
}

value ApiResponse {
    status: Integer
    body: Json
    next: Cursor?
    prev: Cursor?
}

-- What the UI may know about who is logged in.
value SessionSummary {
    domain: String
    account: { id: String, acct: String }?
}

-- Serialised as { kind, message, status? } so the UI decodes a closed sum.
value AppError {
    kind: no_session | invalid_domain | network | http | protocol
        | unsupported | storage | login_aborted
        | decode            -- raised only by the UI's own decoders
    message: String
    status: Integer?        -- http only
}

value Page<T> {
    items: List<T>
    next: Cursor?
    prev: Cursor?
}

-- One file for POST /api/v2/media. The bytes are the raw IPC body (D20).
value MediaUpload {
    bytes: Bytes
    filename: String
    mime: String
    description: String?
}

-- RFC 7636. The verifier never leaves Rust.
value Pkce {
    verifier: String        -- 32 random bytes, base64url without padding (43 characters)
    challenge: String       -- base64url(SHA-256(verifier))
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

-- crates/pixelfed-core. No UI, no webview, no Tauri. Everything that
-- touches the network or the token.
contract Core {
    probe: (domain: Domain) -> InstanceProbe | AppError
    login_begin: (domain: Domain) -> PendingLogin | AppError
    login_finish: (pending: PendingLogin) -> SessionSummary | AppError
    logout: () -> () | AppError
    api_request: (request: ApiRequest) -> ApiResponse | AppError
    api_follow: (url: String) -> ApiResponse | AppError
    media_upload: (upload: MediaUpload) -> ApiResponse | AppError
    session_summary: () -> SessionSummary?

    @invariant ApiPathsOnly
        -- api_request refuses a path not starting with /api/ before any
        -- network activity (api::request_url).

    @invariant UploadsBounded
        -- media_upload refuses an empty body and a body over
        -- max_upload_bytes before any network activity (api::upload); the
        -- instance's own limit is applied by the UI before the bytes are
        -- read and by the server after.

    @invariant PkceAlways
        -- login_begin generates a fresh Pkce; authorize_url carries
        -- code_challenge and code_challenge_method=S256; exchange_code
        -- sends code_verifier (oauth::Pkce, tested against RFC 7636
        -- appendix B).

    @invariant CursorsValidated
        -- api_follow parses the URL and requires https, the session
        -- domain's host and port, and a path under /api/ (api::follow_url,
        -- Domain::owns).

    @invariant RedirectsDropTheToken
        -- reqwest follows at most five redirects and removes Authorization
        -- when the host changes; the client is built with that policy.

    @invariant ErrorsAreTyped
        -- Every failure is an AppError variant. A non-2xx answer becomes
        -- http with the server's error or message field, or the first 200
        -- characters of the body.

    @guidance
        -- Modules: domain, instance (nodeinfo probe, version floor
        -- 0.12.3), oauth (apps, Pkce, authorize URL, loopback listener,
        -- token exchange), link (RFC 8288 parser honouring quotes), api
        -- (request_url, follow_url, send, upload: reqwest multipart with
        -- Part file_name and mime_str, plus a description part when
        -- given), session, store (SecretStore, FileStore), core (Core,
        -- PendingLogin). User agent Pellucid/<version>
        -- (+https://harryprayiv.com). Request timeout 30 s, which bounds
        -- an upload too; login timeout 10 min.
}

-- Where the session is persisted.
contract SecretStore {
    load: () -> Session? | AppError
    save: (session: Session) -> () | AppError
    clear: () -> () | AppError

    @invariant DesktopFileIsPrivate
        -- FileStore writes <app data dir>/session.json through a temporary
        -- file with mode 0600 and renames it into place; load tolerates a
        -- missing file and reports a corrupt one as storage.

    @guidance
        -- Mobile stores are not written. The trait is the only thing a
        -- platform store has to implement.
}

-- src-tauri. The IPC the webview sees. Command names and payloads are the
-- whole of what App.Backend.Tauri knows.
contract Shell {
    session_get: () -> SessionSummary?
    instance_probe: (domain: String) -> InstanceProbe | AppError
    login_start: (domain: String) -> { authorize_url: String } | AppError
    logout: () -> () | AppError
    api_request: (request: ApiRequest) -> ApiResponse | AppError
    api_follow: (url: String) -> ApiResponse | AppError
    media_upload: (body: Bytes, headers: { x-filename, x-mime, x-description }) -> ApiResponse | AppError

    event session-changed: SessionSummary?
    event login-failed: AppError

    @invariant NoProtocolLogic
        -- Each command calls one Core method; the only extra behaviour is
        -- opening the system browser (login_start), emitting the two
        -- events, and unpacking the raw body and percent-decoding the
        -- three headers of media_upload. A JSON body on media_upload is
        -- refused as protocol; a missing filename becomes "upload", a
        -- missing MIME type application/octet-stream, an empty
        -- description none.

    @invariant TokenAbsent
        -- No command result and no event payload contains access_token,
        -- client_secret or refresh_token (D3).

    @guidance
        -- tauri.conf.json: withGlobalTauri true; CSP default-src 'self';
        -- script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' https: data:
        -- blob:; media-src https: blob:; connect-src ipc:
        -- http://ipc.localhost; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none';
        -- base-uri 'none'. Capability default: core:default only.
        -- Plugins: opener (used from Rust, so it needs no capability).
        -- beforeDevCommand { script: "mkdir -p dist && cp static/index.html
        -- static/style.css dist/ && spago bundle", wait: true }.
}

-- src/App/Backend.purs: the record every screen uses. One field per Shell
-- command plus the two subscriptions. App.Backend.Tauri implements it.
contract Backend {
    sessionGet: () -> Aff (Either AppError (Maybe SessionSummary))
    instanceProbe: (domain: String) -> Aff (Either AppError InstanceProbe)
    loginStart: (domain: String) -> Aff (Either AppError LoginStarted)
    logout: () -> Aff (Either AppError Unit)
    apiRequest: (request: ApiRequest) -> Aff (Either AppError ApiResponse)
    apiFollow: (cursor: Cursor) -> Aff (Either AppError ApiResponse)
    mediaUpload: (upload: MediaUpload) -> Aff (Either AppError ApiResponse)
    onSessionChanged: (handler) -> Effect (Effect Unit)
    onLoginFailed: (handler) -> Effect (Effect Unit)

    @invariant NeverThrows
        -- Both foreign invokes resolve to { ok, value } or { ok, error }
        -- and never reject; a thrown exception, an IPC rejection, an
        -- AppError and an undecodable payload all become Left AppError.
        -- Reading a File's bytes is the one Aff that may throw, and the
        -- composer catches it (MediaUploaded).

    @guidance
        -- A second implementation over fetch would serve a Pellucid server
        -- that sets CORS headers. It is not written and nothing depends on
        -- it; the seam exists so that screens never import the Tauri
        -- module.
}

-- D7. Every foreign module in the frontend, with what it supplies.
contract ForeignBudget {
    App.Backend.Tauri.js: invokeImpl, invokeRawImpl (Uint8Array body, percent-encoded headers), listenImpl over window.__TAURI__
    Util.File.js: arrayBufferImpl, file.arrayBuffer()

    @invariant Named
        -- A foreign module not listed here is not in the tree. Test
        -- fixtures are read by test/Test/Main.js, which is test code and
        -- not shipped.
}

-- The routes the client uses, as pixelfed-rn calls them.
contract PixelfedApi {
    nodeinfo:            GET  /api/nodeinfo/2.0.json
    register_app:        POST /api/v1/apps                               form
    authorize:           GET  /oauth/authorize                            browser
    token:               POST /oauth/token                                form
    verify:              GET  /api/v1/accounts/verify_credentials         _pe
    home:                GET  /api/v1/timelines/home                      _pe limit=20   Link
    public:              GET  /api/v1/timelines/public                    _pe limit=20   Link
    status:              GET  /api/v1/statuses/{id}                       _pe
    context:             GET  /api/v1/statuses/{id}/context               _pe            no Link, 100 max
    favourite:           POST /api/v1/statuses/{id}/favourite             _pe            Pixelfed entity
    unfavourite:         POST /api/v1/statuses/{id}/unfavourite           _pe            Pixelfed entity
    bookmark:            POST /api/v1/statuses/{id}/bookmark              _pe ignored    Mastodon entity
    unbookmark:          POST /api/v1/statuses/{id}/unbookmark            _pe ignored    Mastodon entity
    reply:               POST /api/v1/statuses                            _pe  body { status, in_reply_to_id, visibility, sensitive }
    create:              POST /api/v1/statuses                            _pe  body { status, media_ids, visibility, sensitive, comments_disabled, spoiler_text? }
    delete:              DELETE /api/v1/statuses/{id}                                    comments and own posts
    account:             GET  /api/v1/accounts/{id}                       _pe
    account_statuses:    GET  /api/v1/accounts/{id}/statuses              _pe limit=24 [max_id]   no Link
    relationships:       GET  /api/v1/accounts/relationships?id[]=        _pe
    follow:              POST /api/v1/accounts/{id}/follow
    unfollow:            POST /api/v1/accounts/{id}/unfollow
    notifications:       GET  /api/v1/notifications                       _pe limit=20   Link, server cap 40
    compose_settings:    GET  /api/v1.1/compose/settings
    media_upload:        POST /api/v2/media                               multipart file [description]   Rust only
    media_update:        PUT  /api/v1/media/{id}                          body { description }

    @invariant EveryReadAsksForThePixelfedEntity
        -- Every GET above carries _pe=1 (Pixelfed.Client pixelfedEntity),
        -- except compose_settings, which is not an entity read.

    @guidance
        -- spoiler_text is sent only when non-empty after trimming, so a
        -- post that is not sensitive never carries one. Routes pixelfed-rn
        -- uses that are not here are the NOT BUILT surfaces: search
        -- (/api/v2/search), discover (/api/v1.1/discover/*), hashtags,
        -- conversations and /api/v1.1/direct/*, followers and following
        -- (Pixelfed's cursor= pagination, a third scheme), stories
        -- (/api/v1.2/stories/*), settings, admin, and notification
        -- filtering by types[].
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum Method { GET | POST | PUT | DELETE }

-- Unknown values are kept, not rejected (D8).
enum Visibility { public | unlisted | private | direct | draft | other(String) }

enum PfType {
    photo
    | photo_album
    | video
    | video_album
    | photo_video_album
    | share
    | text
    | other(String)
}

enum MediaType { image | video | gifv | audio | unknown }

-- Hash routes: #/, #/public, #/notifications, #/compose, #/profile/{id},
-- #/status/{id}.
enum Route { home | public | notifications | compose | profile(AccountId) | status_detail(StatusId) }

-- NotificationTransformer::replaceTypeVerb output; unknown verbs kept (D8).
enum NotificationKind {
    follow | mention | share | favourite | comment | tagged | modlog
    | direct | story_react | story_comment | other(String)
}

-- One picked file in the composer. rejected covers both a local refusal
-- (too large, type not allowed) and a failed upload, with the reason.
enum ItemPhase { uploading | uploaded(MediaAttachment) | rejected(String) }

enum Posting { idle | posting | failed(String) }

enum Deletion { not_armed | armed | deleting }

enum Phase { booting | boot_failed(String) | logged_out | logged_in(SessionSummary) }

enum LoginPhase { entering | working | waiting(LoginStarted) | failed(AppError) }

enum FeedState { loading | failed(AppError) | loaded }

enum MoreState { idle | loading_more | more_failed(AppError) | exhausted }

enum Toggle { favourite | bookmark }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rust side only (D3).
entity Session {
    domain: Domain
    client_id: String
    client_secret: String
    access_token: String
    refresh_token: String?
    account: { id: String, acct: String }?
}

-- A login that has begun: the port is bound, the client registered, the
-- browser opened, the code not yet received.
entity PendingLogin {
    domain: Domain
    client_id: String
    client_secret: String
    redirect_uri: String
    state: String            -- UUID v4, simple form
    pkce: Pkce
    authorize_url: String
}

entity Account {
    id: AccountId
    username: String
    acct: String
    display_name: String
    note: String             -- HTML, never rendered as such
    note_text: String?
    url: String
    avatar: String
    locked: Boolean
    followers_count: Integer
    following_count: Integer
    statuses_count: Integer
    local: Boolean
    is_admin: Boolean
    created_at: String
    website: String?
    header_bg: String?
    pronouns: List<String>
    has_story: Boolean
}

entity MediaAttachment {
    id: MediaId
    type: MediaType
    url: String
    preview_url: String?
    optimized_url: String?
    description: String?
    blurhash: String?
    is_nsfw: Boolean
    mime: String?
    dimensions: { width: Integer, height: Integer }?   -- meta.original
}

entity Status {
    id: StatusId
    uri: String
    url: String?
    created_at: String
    edited_at: String?
    account: Account
    content: String          -- HTML, never rendered as such
    content_text: String?
    visibility: Visibility
    sensitive: Boolean
    spoiler_text: String
    pf_type: PfType
    media_attachments: List<MediaAttachment>
    favourites_count: Integer
    reblogs_count: Integer
    reply_count: Integer
    favourited: Boolean
    reblogged: Boolean
    bookmarked: Boolean
    comments_disabled: Boolean
    in_reply_to_id: StatusId?
    in_reply_to_account_id: AccountId?
    reblog: Status?
    tags: List<{ name: String, url: String }>
    mentions: List<{ id: AccountId, username: String, acct: String, url: String }>
    liked_by: { id: AccountId?, username: String?, others: Boolean, total_count: Integer }?
    place: { name: String, country: String? }?
    local: Boolean
    pinned: Boolean

    -- The status whose media and caption are shown: reblog when present.
    let displayed = reblog or this
}

entity Relationship {
    id: AccountId
    following: Boolean
    followed_by: Boolean
    blocking: Boolean
    muting: Boolean
    requested: Boolean
}

entity Root {
    phase: Phase
    route: Route
}

-- One timeline screen (home or public).
entity Feed {
    kind: home | public
    state: FeedState
    statuses: List<Status>
    next: Cursor?
    more: MoreState
    now: Instant?
    revealed: Set<StatusId>
    busy: Set<StatusId>
    notice: String?
}

entity Detail {
    id: StatusId
    me: AccountId?
    main: pending | missing(AppError) | ready(Status)
    comments: pending | missing(AppError) | ready(List<Status>)
    reply: { text: String, sending: Boolean, error: String? }
    deletion: Deletion
    revealed: Set<StatusId>
    busy: Set<StatusId>
    notice: String?

    -- The displayed post belongs to the viewer.
    let is_mine = main is ready and main.displayed.account.id = me
}

entity Profile {
    id: AccountId
    me: AccountId?
    account: pending | missing(AppError) | ready(Account)
    relationship: Relationship?
    relationship_busy: Boolean
    posts: List<Status>
    posts_phase: loading | idle | exhausted | failed(AppError)
    notice: String?

    let is_self = me = id
}

-- One entry of GET /api/v1/notifications. account is the actor; it,
-- status and tagged are optional because the server drops what it can no
-- longer load and because a part that fails to decode must not take the
-- row with it (D8).
entity Notification {
    id: NotificationId
    kind: NotificationKind
    created_at: String
    account: Account?
    status: Status?
    tagged: { username: String, status_id: StatusId }?
}

-- GET /api/v1.1/compose/settings. Sizes are kilobytes, as Laravel's max:
-- rule counts uploads.
entity ComposeSettings {
    allowed_media_types: List<String>      -- empty means the server did not say
    max_caption_length: Integer
    max_file_size_kb: Integer
    max_media_attachments: Integer
    max_alt_text_length: Integer
    default_visibility: Visibility?
}

-- What the composer sends to create.
entity NewPost {
    caption: String
    media_ids: List<MediaId>
    visibility: Visibility
    sensitive: Boolean
    spoiler_text: String
    comments_disabled: Boolean
}

entity Notifications {
    list: loading | failed(AppError) | loaded
    items: List<Notification>
    next: Cursor?
    more: MoreState
    now: Instant?
}

-- One picked file in the composer.
entity ComposeItem {
    key: Integer
    name: String
    mime: String
    size_bytes: Number
    phase: ItemPhase
    alt_text: String
    alt_saved: String        -- the description the server holds
    alt_busy: Boolean
    alt_error: String?
}

entity Compose {
    settings: ComposeSettings
    items: List<ComposeItem>
    next_key: Integer
    caption: String
    visibility: Visibility   -- public, unlisted or private
    sensitive: Boolean
    spoiler_text: String
    comments_disabled: Boolean
    posting: Posting
    notice: String?

    let uploaded_ids = items where phase is uploaded, their attachment ids
    let can_post = items != [] and every item.phase is uploaded
                   and no item.alt_busy and posting != posting
                   and length(caption) <= settings.max_caption_length
                   and (not sensitive or length(spoiler_text) <= max_spoiler_length)
}

entity KnownIssue {
    name: String
    status: open | closed
    effect: String
    closes_when: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    min_pixelfed_version: String = "0.12.3"
    scopes: String = "read write follow push"
    client_name: String = "Pellucid"
    client_website: String = "https://harryprayiv.com"
    identifier: String = "com.harryprayiv.pellucid"
    request_timeout: Duration = 30.seconds
    login_timeout: Duration = 10.minutes
    max_redirects: Integer = 5
    feed_page: Integer = 20
    profile_page: Integer = 24
    notifications_page: Integer = 20          -- the server caps it at 40
    relationship_batch_max: Integer = 20
    session_file: String = "session.json"
    session_file_mode: String = "0600"
    max_upload_bytes: Integer = 536870912     -- 512 MiB, Rust's ceiling before the instance's own
    max_spoiler_length: Integer = 140         -- POST /api/v1/statuses validation
    pkce_verifier_bytes: Integer = 32
    -- Pixelfed's stock values, used when compose_settings cannot be read.
    default_allowed_media_types: List<String> = ["image/jpeg", "image/jpg", "image/png", "image/gif"]
    default_max_caption_length: Integer = 500
    default_max_file_size_kb: Integer = 15000
    default_max_media_attachments: Integer = 4
    default_max_alt_text_length: Integer = 1000
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Defaults
------------------------------------------------------------

default KnownIssue no_token_revoke = {
    name: "logout does not revoke the token on the server",
    status: open,
    effect: "a token copied out of session.json before logout stays valid until the instance expires it; the person can only revoke it from the instance's own settings page",
    closes_when: "the server offers a route that revokes the caller's own token. Stock Pixelfed does not: Passport ships no RFC 7009 /oauth/revoke, DELETE /oauth/tokens/{id} needs the browser session, and /api/v1.1/accounts/apps-and-applications/{id}/revoke answers 422 for the current token. A Pellucid server will offer one; against Pixelfed this stays open"
}

default KnownIssue orphan_uploads = {
    name: "an upload removed from the composer, or abandoned with it, stays on the server",
    status: open,
    effect: "media uploaded through POST /api/v2/media and never attached to a status counts against the account's daily upload limit and storage until Pixelfed's media garbage collector removes it",
    closes_when: "removing an uploaded item sends DELETE /api/v1/media/{id} where the instance supports it, and leaving the composer with uploads asks first"
}

default KnownIssue smoke_harness_external = {
    name: "the headless UI run is not in the repository",
    status: open,
    effect: "scripts/check.fish does not run it; the 105 checks that exercise login, feeds, detail, profile, notifications, compose and deletion against a mock of the Shell contract exist only where the port was written, so a change can pass the gate and break a screen",
    closes_when: "the harness and its jsdom dependency come from nixpkgs into test/smoke and check.fish runs it after spago bundle"
}

default KnownIssue mobile_store_missing = {
    name: "no SecretStore for Android or iOS",
    status: open,
    effect: "the mobile shells cannot persist a session; a phone build would ask for login on every start",
    closes_when: "a Kotlin and a Swift store behind the SecretStore trait, exercised by the same round-trip test FileStore has"
}

default KnownIssue deep_link_unwritten = {
    name: "the mobile redirect branch of D10 is not written",
    status: open,
    effect: "a phone build cannot complete login; the loopback listener is unreachable from a system browser on Android and iOS",
    closes_when: "tauri-plugin-deep-link registers a scheme, the redirect URI registered in /api/v1/apps is that scheme on mobile, and on_open_url hands the code and state to login_finish"
}

default KnownIssue tauri_shell_uncompiled = {
    name: "src-tauri was reviewed against crate sources, not compiled, when this spec was written",
    status: open,
    effect: "a typo in src-tauri surfaces on the first cargo tauri dev rather than before delivery",
    closes_when: "cargo clippy -p pellucid -- -D warnings has run clean in the dev shell on winsmuth"
}

default KnownIssue android_shell_untested = {
    name: "the android devShell has never been entered",
    status: open,
    effect: "SDK, NDK and build-tools versions in flake.nix are a first guess",
    closes_when: "cargo tauri android init and cargo tauri android dev succeed from that shell on winsmuth"
}

default KnownIssue lab_instance_undeployed = {
    name: "pixelfed-lab.nix has been parsed but not built or deployed",
    status: open,
    effect: "the client has only been exercised against a mock of the Shell contract and against the reading of the server's source",
    closes_when: "./build boot blade with the module imported, a user created with pixelfed-manage, and one login plus one home timeline fetched from Pellucid"
}

default KnownIssue feeds_end_in_a_button = {
    name: "no infinite scroll",
    status: open,
    effect: "each feed and the profile grid stop at a Load more button",
    closes_when: "an IntersectionObserver sentinel below the list triggers LoadMore while more is idle, with the button kept as the fallback"
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Session ----------------------------------------------------------------

rule SessionRestored {
    when: AppStarted()
    ensures:
        shell.core.session = shell.store.load()
        ui.root.route = ParsedHash() or home
        ui.root.phase = if shell.session_get() = null: logged_out
                        else: logged_in(shell.session_get())

    @guidance
        -- Root subscribes to session-changed and to hash changes before it
        -- asks for the session, so nothing emitted during boot is missed.
        -- A storage error at load is shown as boot_failed with the
        -- message; it is the one state with no button, since the fix is
        -- outside the app.
}

rule LoginStarted {
    when: LoginSubmitted(domain_text)
    requires: trim(domain_text) != ""
    requires: ui.login.phase != working
    let domain = Domain.parse(domain_text)
    ensures:
        if domain is AppError:
            ui.login.phase = failed(domain)
        else:
            instance.probed                                  -- nodeinfo, floor 0.12.3
            pending = PendingLogin{ listener bound on 127.0.0.1:0,
                                    client registered with redirect_uri = that port,
                                    state = fresh UUID,
                                    pkce = fresh Pkce }
            pending.authorize_url carries client_id, redirect_uri, response_type=code,
                scope, state, code_challenge = pkce.challenge, code_challenge_method = S256
            SystemBrowser.opened_url = pending.authorize_url
            ui.login.phase = waiting({ authorize_url })

    @guidance
        -- login_start returns as soon as the browser is opened; the rest
        -- happens in a spawned task. The waiting screen shows the URL as
        -- text for the case where no browser opened.
}

rule LoginCompleted {
    when: RedirectReceived(request_line)
    requires: request_line is GET /callback with state = pending.state and a non-empty code
    ensures:
        listener answered 200 with the "Logged in" page
        token = POST /oauth/token (code, client_id, client_secret, redirect_uri, scope,
                                   code_verifier = pending.pkce.verifier)
        session = Session{ domain, client_id, client_secret, token.access_token, token.refresh_token }
        session.account = GET verify_credentials?_pe=1 → { id, acct }
        shell.store.save(session)
        shell.core.session = session
        Emitted(session-changed, session.summary)
        ui.root.phase = logged_in(summary)
        ui.root.route = home

    @guidance
        -- A request with the wrong state, another path or a method other
        -- than GET is answered 404 and the listener keeps waiting; an
        -- error parameter ends the login with login_aborted. The code is
        -- used once; the listener closes after the first accepted request.
}

rule LoginFailed {
    when: LoginTaskEnded(error)
    ensures:
        Emitted(login-failed, error)
        ui.login.phase = failed(error)

    @guidance
        -- Covers the timeout (10 minutes without a redirect), a refused
        -- token exchange, a failed verify_credentials and a store that
        -- cannot be written. The domain field keeps its text.
}

rule LoggedOut {
    when: LogoutPressed()
    ensures:
        shell.store.clear()
        shell.core.session = null
        Emitted(session-changed, null)
        ui.root.phase = logged_out
        ui.root.route = home

    @guidance
        -- When clear fails the UI still moves to logged_out: the file
        -- could not be removed, which is reported, but the person asked
        -- to leave. KnownIssue no_token_revoke.
}

-- Transport --------------------------------------------------------------

rule RequestSent {
    when: ApiRequested(request)
    requires: shell.core.session != null
    requires: request.path starts with "/api/"
    let url = session.domain.base_url + request.path + query
    ensures:
        Sent(request.method, url,
             headers: Authorization Bearer token, Accept application/json,
             body as JSON when present)
        response = ApiResponse{ status, body parsed as JSON or null when empty,
                                next and prev from the Link header }
        or AppError.http(status, message) when status is not 2xx
        or AppError.protocol when the body is not JSON

    @guidance
        -- No session: no_session before any network activity. A path
        -- outside /api/: protocol, before any network activity.
}

rule CursorFollowed {
    when: CursorFollowed(cursor)
    requires: shell.core.session != null
    requires: cursor.url parses, scheme = https, host and port = session.domain, path starts with "/api/"
    ensures:
        RequestSent(GET cursor.url) with the same headers as RequestSent

    @guidance
        -- A cursor that fails the check is protocol with the offending
        -- URL in the message. The UI never builds or edits a cursor.
}

-- Feeds ------------------------------------------------------------------

rule FeedLoads {
    when: FeedOpened(kind) or FeedRefreshed(kind)
    ensures:
        feed.state = loading
        feed.now = Now()
        page = GET (home | public) timeline ?_pe=1&limit=20
        if page is AppError: feed.state = failed(page)
        else:
            feed.statuses = page.items
            feed.next = page.next
            feed.more = idle
            feed.state = loaded

    @guidance
        -- Switching between Home and Public reuses one component; a new
        -- kind resets the feed and loads. Refresh clears the notice.
}

rule FeedLoadsMore {
    when: LoadMorePressed()
    requires: feed.state = loaded and feed.next != null
    requires: feed.more in { idle, more_failed }
    ensures:
        feed.more = loading_more
        page = CursorFollowed(feed.next)
        if page is AppError: feed.more = more_failed(page)
        else:
            fresh = page.items without ids already in feed.statuses
            feed.statuses = feed.statuses ++ fresh
            feed.next = page.next
            feed.more = if fresh = [] or page.next = null: exhausted else: idle
            feed.now = Now()

    @guidance
        -- A page with no new ids ends the list even when the server
        -- offers another cursor, which stops a loop on a server that
        -- repeats itself.
}

rule ToggleApplied {
    when: TogglePressed(id, toggle)                 -- on a feed, the detail post or a comment
    requires: id not in busy
    let target = the displayed status with that id on this screen
    ensures:
        busy includes id
        answer = POST favourite|unfavourite|bookmark|unbookmark by target's current flag, ?_pe=1
        busy excludes id
        if answer is AppError: notice = message
        else:
            merged = if toggle = favourite: answer
                     else: target with bookmarked = answer.bookmarked
            every list on the screen replaces the status with that id by merged,
                whether it sits at the top level or inside a share wrapper

    @guidance
        -- Pixelfed.StatusOps holds request, merge, replaceDisplayed and
        -- replaceAll; Feed and StatusDetail hold only the state glue. The
        -- card shows the old state while busy and disables the two
        -- buttons.
}

rule SensitiveRevealed {
    when: ShowPressed(id)
    ensures:
        revealed includes id
        the card's media block is drawn in place of the cover

    @guidance
        -- Media of a sensitive post is not requested until revealed: the
        -- cover is a div with the spoiler text and one button. The set is
        -- per screen and resets with it.
}

-- Post detail ------------------------------------------------------------

rule DetailOpens {
    when: RouteChanged(status_detail(id))
    ensures:
        detail.main = pending; detail.comments = pending
        in parallel:
            main = GET /api/v1/statuses/{id}?_pe=1
            context = GET /api/v1/statuses/{id}/context?_pe=1
        detail.main = ready(main) or missing(error)
        detail.comments = ready(context.descendants) or missing(error)
        the main card is drawn with its Comments button disabled
        the reply form is drawn unless main.comments_disabled

    @guidance
        -- Comments are the descendants, flat, in server order. Ancestors
        -- are fetched and not shown (a comment opened as a post has no
        -- parent link yet). A Back header action calls history.back().
}

rule ReplyPosted {
    when: ReplySubmitted(text)
    requires: detail.main = ready(main)
    requires: trim(text) != "" and not detail.reply.sending
    ensures:
        detail.reply.sending = true
        answer = POST /api/v1/statuses?_pe=1
                 body { status: text, in_reply_to_id: main.displayed.id, visibility: "public", sensitive: false }
        if answer is AppError: detail.reply = { text, sending: false, error: message }
        else:
            detail.comments = ready(comments ++ [answer])
            detail.reply = { text: "", sending: false, error: null }
            main.displayed.reply_count += 1
}

rule CommentDeleted {
    when: DeletePressed(comment_id)
    requires: comment.account.id = me
    requires: comment_id not in busy
    ensures:
        busy includes comment_id
        answer = DELETE /api/v1/statuses/{comment_id}
        busy excludes comment_id
        if answer is AppError: notice = message
        else:
            detail.comments = ready(comments without comment_id)
            main.displayed.reply_count -= 1, not below 0

    @guidance
        -- The delete button exists only on the viewer's own comments and
        -- sends at once; a comment is cheap to repost. The main post is
        -- rule PostDeleted, which asks first.
}

rule PostDeleted {
    when: DeletePressed() then ConfirmPressed()
    requires: detail.is_mine
    requires: detail.deletion = not_armed at the first press, armed at the second
    ensures:
        after DeletePressed: detail.deletion = armed, the confirmation strip is drawn, nothing sent
        after KeepPressed: detail.deletion = not_armed
        after ConfirmPressed:
            detail.deletion = deleting
            answer = DELETE /api/v1/statuses/{main.displayed.id}
            if answer is AppError: detail.deletion = not_armed; notice = message
            else: history.back()

    @guidance
        -- The delete action sits in the header and exists only when
        -- is_mine; for a share it refers to the displayed post, which is
        -- the viewer's when the viewer's post was boosted by someone else.
        -- Reload disarms. The feed or grid the person returns to still
        -- holds the deleted post until it reloads (NOT BUILT: local
        -- removal across screens).
}

-- Notifications ----------------------------------------------------------

rule NotificationsLoad {
    when: NotificationsOpened() or NotificationsRefreshed()
    ensures:
        notifications.list = loading
        notifications.now = Now()
        page = GET /api/v1/notifications?_pe=1&limit=20
        if page is AppError: notifications.list = failed(page)
        else:
            notifications.items = page.items
            notifications.next = page.next
            notifications.more = idle
            notifications.list = loaded

    @guidance
        -- Decoding is per row: a row whose account, status or tagged part
        -- does not decode keeps the row with that part absent; only a row
        -- without an id fails the page (Pixelfed.Decode decodeNotification).
}

rule NotificationsLoadMore {
    when: LoadMorePressed()
    requires: notifications.list = loaded and notifications.next != null
    requires: notifications.more in { idle, more_failed }
    ensures:
        notifications.more = loading_more
        page = CursorFollowed(notifications.next)
        if page is AppError: notifications.more = more_failed(page)
        else:
            fresh = page.items without ids already held
            notifications.items = notifications.items ++ fresh
            notifications.next = page.next
            notifications.more = if fresh = [] or page.next = null: exhausted else: idle
            notifications.now = Now()
}

rule NotificationOpened {
    when: RowPressed(notification)
    let target =
        if kind = tagged and tagged != null: status_detail(tagged.status_id)
        else if kind = comment and status != null: status_detail(status.in_reply_to_id or status.id)
        else if status != null: status_detail(status.displayed.id)
        else if account != null: profile(account.id)
        else: none
    requires: target != none                      -- a row with no target is drawn disabled
    ensures:
        RouteChanged(target)

    @guidance
        -- The avatar is its own button and always opens the actor. The
        -- row reads "<actor> <phrase>" with the phrases pixelfed-rn uses:
        -- followed you, mentioned you, shared your post, liked your post,
        -- commented on your post, tagged you in a post, left a moderation
        -- note, sent you a message, reacted to your story, commented on
        -- your story; an unknown verb is shown as received. Below it, one
        -- line of the status concerned (a comment's or mention's own text,
        -- otherwise the caption of the liked or shared post), and to the
        -- right the first attachment's preview, blank when the post is
        -- sensitive. "Someone" stands in for a missing actor.
}

-- Compose ----------------------------------------------------------------

rule ComposeOpens {
    when: RouteChanged(compose)
    ensures:
        compose = Compose{ settings: defaults, items: [], visibility: public, posting: idle }
        answer = GET /api/v1.1/compose/settings
        if answer is AppError: notice = "Using default upload limits. " + message
        else:
            compose.settings = answer
            compose.visibility = answer.default_visibility when it is public, unlisted or private

    @guidance
        -- The picker's accept attribute is the allowed types joined by
        -- commas, absent when the server listed none. multiple is set
        -- while more than one slot is free; the picker disappears when
        -- none is. The limits line reads "Up to N files, M MB each" with
        -- M = max_file_size_kb / 1000, as Pixelfed shows it.
}

rule MediaPicked {
    when: FilesChosen(files)
    let room = settings.max_media_attachments - length(items)
    ensures:
        the input's value is cleared so the same file can be chosen again
        if length(files) > room: notice names how many were left out
        for file in the first room files:
            item = ComposeItem{ key: next_key, name: file.name, mime: file.type or application/octet-stream,
                                size_bytes: file.size, alt_text: "", alt_saved: "" }
            item.phase =
                if file.size > settings.max_file_size_kb * 1024: rejected("Larger than M MB")
                else if settings.allowed_media_types != [] and item.mime not in them:
                    rejected("This server does not accept <mime>")
                else: uploading
            items = items ++ [item]; next_key += 1
            if item.phase = uploading: MediaUploaded(item, file) in its own fiber

    @guidance
        -- The size and type checks are the server's own rules applied
        -- early, so a 15 MB limit is not discovered after a 15 MB
        -- transfer. The browser's MIME type comes from the extension; the
        -- server sniffs the content, so it has the last word and its
        -- refusal lands in the same rejected state.
}

rule MediaUploaded {
    when: MediaUploaded(item, file)
    ensures:
        bytes = file.arrayBuffer()              -- a failure to read is rejected("Could not read the file: ...")
        answer = Shell.media_upload(bytes, x-filename: file.name, x-mime: item.mime, x-description: "")
                 = Core.media_upload = POST /api/v2/media multipart
        item.phase = if answer is AppError: rejected(message) else: uploaded(answer as MediaAttachment)

    @guidance
        -- The attachment decodes with url null and preview_url set; the
        -- decoder falls back to preview_url for url, and the thumbnail
        -- is preview_url. Removing an item only drops the row (KnownIssue
        -- orphan_uploads); an upload in flight for a removed row still
        -- completes and its answer is ignored because no row has its key.
}

rule AltTextSaved {
    when: AltTextBlurred(item) or PostPressed()
    requires: item.phase = uploaded(m)
    requires: trim(item.alt_text) != item.alt_saved and not item.alt_busy
    ensures:
        item.alt_busy = true
        answer = PUT /api/v1/media/{m.id} body { description: trim(alt_text) }
        item.alt_busy = false
        if answer is AppError: item.alt_error = message
        else: item.alt_saved = answer.description or trim(alt_text); item.alt_error = null

    @guidance
        -- On PostPressed every unsaved alt text is saved in parallel
        -- before the status is created; one failure stops the post with
        -- "Alt text could not be saved. Fix it or remove the file." The
        -- field shows "Saved" when its text equals alt_saved and is not
        -- empty, otherwise its length against max_alt_text_length.
}

rule PostCreated {
    when: PostPressed()
    requires: compose.can_post
    ensures:
        compose.posting = posting
        AltTextSaved for every item that needs it; stop with failed(...) if any fails
        answer = POST /api/v1/statuses?_pe=1 body {
            status: trim(caption), media_ids: uploaded_ids, visibility, sensitive,
            comments_disabled, spoiler_text: trim(spoiler_text) when sensitive and non-empty }
        if answer is AppError: compose.posting = failed(message)
        else: RouteChanged(status_detail(answer.id))

    @guidance
        -- Typing in the caption clears a failed state. The visibility
        -- select offers Public, Unlisted and Followers only (private);
        -- direct is a message, not a post. The content warning field
        -- appears only while sensitive is checked and what it holds is
        -- not sent otherwise. Leaving the screen discards the composer;
        -- there are no drafts.
}

-- Profile ----------------------------------------------------------------

rule ProfileOpens {
    when: RouteChanged(profile(id))
    ensures:
        profile.account = pending
        in parallel:
            account = GET /api/v1/accounts/{id}?_pe=1
            relationship = if is_self: null
                           else: first of GET /api/v1/accounts/relationships?id[]={id}&_pe=1
        profile.account = ready(account) or missing(error)
        profile.relationship = relationship            -- a relationship error is a notice, not a failure
        if account is ready: ProfilePages(max_id: null)

    @guidance
        -- The header shows avatar, counts, display name, acct with a lock
        -- mark when locked, the plain-text bio (note_text, else note
        -- stripped) and the website as text. The follow button is absent
        -- on the viewer's own profile.
}

rule FollowToggled {
    when: FollowPressed()
    requires: profile.relationship = r and not profile.relationship_busy
    ensures:
        profile.relationship_busy = true
        answer = if r.following or r.requested: POST /unfollow else: POST /follow
        profile.relationship_busy = false
        if answer is AppError: notice = message
        else: profile.relationship = answer

    @guidance
        -- Labels: Following when following, Requested when requested,
        -- Follow otherwise; the first two are drawn as secondary buttons.
        -- Unfollow on a requested relationship withdraws the request, as
        -- pixelfed-rn does.
}

rule ProfilePages {
    when: ProfilePages(max_id) or LoadMorePressed()
    requires: profile.posts_phase in { idle, failed } or max_id = null
    ensures:
        profile.posts_phase = loading
        page = GET /api/v1/accounts/{id}/statuses?_pe=1&limit=24[&max_id={last id held}]
        if page is AppError: profile.posts_phase = failed(page)
        else:
            fresh = page without ids already held
            profile.posts = profile.posts ++ fresh
            profile.posts_phase = if fresh = []: exhausted else: idle

    @guidance
        -- The grid is three tiles wide; a tile shows the first attachment's
        -- preview (optimized or original when absent), a play mark for
        -- video, a stack mark for albums, the word Sensitive for a
        -- sensitive post, and a caption excerpt for a text post. A locked
        -- account the viewer does not follow shows "This account is
        -- private." in place of an empty grid.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant TokenNeverCrossesTheBridge {
    for m in ShellMessages:                 -- command results and event payloads
        not Contains(m, session.access_token)
        and not Contains(m, session.client_secret)
        and not Contains(m, session.refresh_token)
}

invariant TokenOnlyToApiPaths {
    for r in SentRequests where r.headers has Authorization:
        r.url.scheme = "https"
        and r.url.host = session.domain.host and r.url.port = session.domain.port
        and r.url.path starts with "/api/"
}

invariant NoHtmlInjection {
    for n in RenderedNodes:
        not UsesInnerHtml(n)
}

invariant ForeignBudgetHeld {
    for f in FrontendSources where f.extension = "js":
        f in ForeignBudget or f under "test/"
}

invariant HttpsOnly {
    for d in Domains:
        d.base_url starts with "https://"
}

invariant WarningFreeBuild {
    -- D15. scripts/check.fish is the executable form of this invariant.
    for b in Builds where b.delivered:
        b.purs_warnings = 0 and b.clippy_warnings = 0 and b.tidy_clean and b.fmt_clean
}

invariant ServerIsTruthForToggles {
    for t in Toggles:
        t.shown_state changes only when t.answer arrives
}

invariant LenientDecodersKeepTheFeed {
    for s in ServerStatuses:
        Decodes(s) unless s lacks id, uri, created_at or account.{id, username, acct, url}
}

invariant PagesNeverRepeat {
    for l in StatusLists:
        Unique(l.map(statusId))
    for l in NotificationLists:
        Unique(l.map(id))
}

invariant NoPostWithoutMedia {
    -- D21. The server's rule, held on the client so the 403 is never seen.
    for c in StatusCreates where c.in_reply_to_id = null:
        c.media_ids != []
}

invariant BytesCrossOnce {
    -- D20. A picked file is read once, sent once and never written.
    for u in MediaUploads:
        u.read_count = 1 and u.ipc_body_is_raw and not u.touched_disk_in_shell
}

invariant VerifierStaysInRust {
    -- D19.
    for m in ShellMessages:
        not Contains(m, pending.pkce.verifier)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

actor Viewer {
    identified_by: Person where instance.probed
}

actor Developer {
    identified_by: Person where has the repository and the dev shell
}

actor Adopter {
    identified_by: Person where runs their own instance
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface LoginScreen {
    facing viewer: Viewer

    exposes:
        ui.login.phase
        ui.login.authorize_url when waiting

    provides:
        LoginStarted(domain_text) when phase in { entering, failed }
        Reset() when phase = waiting

    contracts:
        demands Shell
        demands Core

    @guarantee NoEmbeddedLogin
        -- The password is typed into the system browser on the instance's
        -- own page, never into the app.

    @guarantee NothingLeaksOnFailure
        -- A failed login leaves no session file and no partial session in
        -- memory; the registered client is abandoned on the server.
}

surface Feed {
    facing viewer: Viewer

    exposes:
        feed.statuses as cards: boost line, avatar, names, age, media or
            sensitive cover, like with count, comments with count, bookmark,
            spoiler, caption, place
        feed.more
        feed.notice

    provides:
        FeedLoads(kind) via the Home and Public tabs and the Refresh button
        FeedLoadsMore() when feed.next != null and feed.more in { idle, more_failed }
        ToggleApplied(id, favourite | bookmark)
        SensitiveRevealed(id)
        RouteChanged(profile(account_id)) from avatar and name
        RouteChanged(status_detail(id)) from the comments button

    contracts:
        demands Backend
        demands PixelfedApi

    @guidance
        -- The card is a render function (View.StatusCard), not a
        -- component; the feed owns revealed and busy. The album layout is
        -- a scroll-snapped row; a single video is a <video controls
        -- playsinline preload=metadata> with the preview as poster.
}

surface PostDetail {
    facing viewer: Viewer

    exposes:
        the post as a card with its comments button disabled
        a delete action in the header when is_mine, and detail.deletion as
            the confirmation strip
        detail.comments as rows: avatar, name, age, text, like with count,
            delete on the viewer's own comments
        detail.reply
        detail.notice

    provides:
        DetailOpens(id)
        ToggleApplied(id, favourite | bookmark) on the post and on comments
        SensitiveRevealed(id)
        ReplyPosted(text) unless comments_disabled
        CommentDeleted(id) when comment.account.id = me
        PostDeleted() when is_mine
        RouteChanged(profile(account_id)) from avatars
        Back()

    contracts:
        demands Backend
        demands PixelfedApi
}

surface Notifications {
    facing viewer: Viewer

    exposes:
        notifications.items as rows: actor avatar, "<actor> <phrase>",
            one line of the post concerned, age, thumbnail
        notifications.more

    provides:
        NotificationsLoad() via the Alerts tab and the Refresh button
        NotificationsLoadMore() when next != null and more in { idle, more_failed }
        NotificationOpened(notification) from the row
        RouteChanged(profile(actor.id)) from the avatar

    contracts:
        demands Backend
        demands PixelfedApi

    @guidance
        -- One list, every type. Pixelfed's types[] filter offers mention,
        -- reblog, follow and favourite and nothing for comments, so a
        -- filter row would be lopsided; it is NOT BUILT.
}

surface Compose {
    facing viewer: Viewer

    exposes:
        compose.items as rows: thumbnail or placeholder, name, state or
            reason, remove, alt text field with counter or Saved
        the picker while a slot is free, and the limits line
        caption with counter, visibility, sensitive, content warning when
            sensitive, comments off
        compose.posting as the Post button's label and the error line
        compose.notice

    provides:
        ComposeOpens() via the Post tab
        MediaPicked(files)
        AltTextSaved(item) on blur
        PostCreated() when can_post
        Back()

    contracts:
        demands Backend
        demands Shell                   -- media_upload is the one raw-body command
        demands PixelfedApi

    @guarantee NothingLeavesWithoutIntent
        -- Bytes leave the device only for a file the person picked, to
        -- the logged-in instance, once (BytesCrossOnce). Nothing is
        -- uploaded on behalf of a draft, a paste or a drop.

    @guidance
        -- The file input is visually hidden inside a labelled drop-zone
        -- look-alike; the label is the control, so it is keyboard
        -- reachable. There is no cropping, filtering, reordering or
        -- location tagging; pixelfed-rn's composer does all four and they
        -- are NOT BUILT.
}

surface Profile {
    facing viewer: Viewer

    exposes:
        profile.account as header: avatar, counts, names, lock, bio, website
        profile.relationship as the follow button, absent when is_self
        profile.posts as a three-wide grid of tiles
        profile.posts_phase
        profile.notice

    provides:
        ProfileOpens(id)
        FollowToggled() when relationship != null and not is_self
        ProfilePages() via Load more
        RouteChanged(status_detail(id)) from a tile
        Back()

    contracts:
        demands Backend
        demands PixelfedApi

    @guidance
        -- The Me tab is this surface with the session's account id.
        -- Followers and following lists are not built; they use Pixelfed's
        -- cursor= pagination, a third scheme.
}

surface DevShell {
    facing developer: Developer

    exposes:
        flake.nix devShells.default: purs, spago, purs-tidy, purs-backend-es,
            purescript-language-server, esbuild, nodejs (the runtime for
            spago test and spago run; no npm packages), rust stable with
            rust-src and rust-analyzer, cargo-tauri, pkg-config,
            gobject-introspection, WebKitGTK 4.1 and GTK 3 and their
            libraries, glib-networking, xdg-utils
        flake.nix devShells.android: the same plus the Android SDK 34, NDK
            26.1.10909125, JDK 17 and the four Android Rust targets (untested)
        scripts/check.fish

    provides:
        nix develop
        spago build, spago test, spago bundle
        cargo tauri icon <png>   -- once; codegen needs icons/32x32.png
        cargo tauri dev          -- runs beforeDevCommand, then the app
        fish scripts/check.fish  -- the gate (D15); bundles into dist/ before the shell step

    @guarantee NoNodeModules
        -- The repository has no package.json; esbuild and node come from
        -- nixpkgs, esbuild driven by spago bundle and node by spago test.

    @guidance
        -- The shell exports XDG_DATA_DIRS with the GTK and gsettings
        -- schemas, GIO_MODULE_DIR for glib-networking (WebKitGTK's TLS for
        -- https images) and WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER=1. The session
        -- file lands in ~/.local/share/com.harryprayiv.pellucid/.
}

surface LabInstance {
    facing developer: Developer

    exposes:
        lab.pixelfed.{enable, domain, acme.{email, dnsProvider, environmentFile}, envSecretFile, openFirewall}
        a Pixelfed 0.12.9 at https://<domain>/ with open registration, no
            email verification, mail to the journal, every ActivityPub switch
            off, OAuth on, EXP_EMC on, the local timeline public

    provides:
        pixelfed-manage user:create --name --username --email --password --is_admin=1 --confirm_email=1
        pixelfed-manage user:admin <username>
        registration in a browser on the LAN for further test accounts

    contracts:
        demands Instance

    @guarantee RealCertificate
        -- Let's Encrypt by DNS-01, so the client's https-only rule (D5)
        -- holds against the lab exactly as it does against
        -- pixelfed.social. The host is never reachable from outside; only
        -- the DNS record is public.

    @guarantee Disposable
        -- Removing the import and /var/lib/pixelfed (and the MySQL
        -- database the module created) leaves nothing behind.

    @guidance
        -- Two sops secrets: APP_KEY=base64:<32 random bytes> for the
        -- instance, and the DNS provider's token under lego's variable
        -- names for the certificate. KnownIssue lab_instance_undeployed.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred OAuth2.authorization_code     -- see: RFC 6749 section 4.1; Pixelfed uses Laravel Passport
deferred Mastodon.api                  -- see: https://docs.joinmastodon.org/methods/
deferred Pixelfed.api                  -- see: app/Http/Controllers/Api/ApiV1Controller.php and routes/api.php in pixelfed/pixelfed
deferred Pixelfed.entities             -- see: app/Transformer/Api/*.php and app/Services/StatusService.php
deferred Tauri.config                  -- see: https://schema.tauri.app/config/2
deferred Tauri.mobile                  -- see: cargo tauri android init, tauri-plugin-deep-link
deferred Nixpkgs.pixelfed              -- see: nixos/modules/services/web-apps/pixelfed.nix
deferred Acme.dns01                    -- see: https://go-acme.github.io/lego/dns/
deferred Pellucid.server               -- see: a future spec; nothing here assumes it

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Whether /api/v1/apps will ever issue a public client, which would let D19 drop the secret from the session file. Today it writes a secret into every client it creates and Passport demands it; a Pellucid server can decide otherwise."
open question "Whether an uploaded item removed from the composer should be deleted on the server at once (KnownIssue orphan_uploads). Pixelfed's API has no documented DELETE /api/v1/media/{id}; its garbage collector removes unattached media after a delay, and a person who removes a file and picks it again would pay the upload twice either way."
open question "Whether deleting a post should also remove it from the feed and grid the person returns to, or whether a reload is enough. Removing it needs a cross-screen signal (a Root-level event or a shared store); reloading costs one request and shows the truth."
open question "Which secret store the Android shell uses: Android Keystore through a small Kotlin plugin, or tauri-plugin-stronghold with a key derived on device. The trait fixes the interface either way."
open question "Whether the lab instance should federate at all. Off keeps it disposable and unreachable; on would let the client be tested against remote accounts and media proxying, which stock instances do constantly."
open question "How hashtags and mentions in captions are linked: from the tags and mentions arrays by text matching, or by a small parser over content that extracts href targets and discards everything else. Both keep D6; the second handles the links Pixelfed inserts for URLs."
open question "Whether the feeds should keep rendering the whole list or window it as nixtune-page does. Twenty posts a page with lazy images is fine for a phone until a session scrolls through hundreds; the point at which it stops being fine is unmeasured."
open question "Whether the name Pellucid collides with a mark in app stores or in the fediverse client space. Nothing was found by hand; a proper check is before D18, not after."
open question "Whether the trust model for the Tauri shell needs a second capability window (an isolation pattern) once the app renders content from many servers, or whether D6 plus the CSP is enough. The isolation pattern costs a second HTML file and a re-review of the IPC."
